:: Mom Desk Calendar [micro_event event nobr] {"position":"1175,3275","size":"100,100"}
/* Desk visitor (micro event 33, "A normal workday" in Define Events): she has filled my work calendar with lunch
   breaks and a time to go home. Shown in the CMD drawer, so no action is spent and there is no exit link.
   Deleting them shows how little it takes now to make her back down. The third choice waits for A Knock at Night. */
<p>$mom.callName comes around to my side of the desk and props her tablet against my monitor, so I have to look at it instead of at whatever I was doing.</p>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs to [
	{ who: $mom, text: "I made a few small changes to your calendar. Tiny ones. You'll barely notice." },
	{ text: "I notice. Every weekday now has a block at noon called LUNCH (REAL FOOD), a fifteen-minute slot at three called 'Stand up and stretch, honey', and at six o'clock, in red, a block that just says HOME. They repeat every week until the end of time, or at least until the end of the calendar app." },
	{ who: $player, text: "You put 'honey' in my work calendar." },
	{ who: $mom, text: "It's your calendar, sweetie, it's not like anybody else can..." },
	{ text: "She leans over my shoulder and reads the sharing settings, which list everybody in the company. Her lips move as she counts the names." },
	{ who: $mom, text: "Oh. Well. Now they know you have a $mom.relation. That's not the worst thing in the world." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>
<br>
<div id="mom-calendar-choice">
	<div>
		<<link "Keep the blocks">>
			<<replace "#mom-calendar-choice">>
				<<silently>>
				<<set _msgs to [
					{ who: $player, text: "Leave them. Take the 'honey' out, though." },
					{ who: $mom, text: "Done. Gone. Not a trace." },
					{ text: "She deletes the word with one finger, very ceremonially, and then stands there smiling at the screen as if I'd agreed to something much bigger than a lunch break." },
				]>>
				<</silently>>
				<<Chat _msgs>>
				<p>The next morning the three o'clock block says 'Stand up and stretch'. The noon block says LUNCH (REAL FOOD, HONEY). I decide that one counts as a compromise.</p>
				<<UpdateStat "+" "MomRelation" 2>>
			<</replace>>
		<</link>>
	</div>
	<div>
		<<link "Have her delete them">>
			<<replace "#mom-calendar-choice">>
				<<silently>>
				<<set _msgs to [
					{ who: $player, text: "My calendar is for meetings. Take them out." },
					{ who: $mom, text: "I just thought, with how late you've been..." },
					{ who: $player, text: "All of them, please." },
					{ who: $mom, text: "Of course. You're right, sweetie. I'll do it now." },
				]>>
				<</silently>>
				<<Chat _msgs>>
				<p>She takes the tablet back and deletes them right there next to my chair, one at a time, with the same care she put into making them. Every recurring block asks if she's sure. Every time, she taps yes.</p>
				<p>Until I was sixteen, she fought me on every single bedtime, and she won most of them. Now it takes two sentences.</p>
				<<UpdateStat "-" "MomRelation" 1>>
				<<UpdateStat "+" "MomCorruption" 1>>
				<<UpdateStat "+" "Efficiency" 1>>
			<</replace>>
		<</link>>
	</div>
	<<if setup.questDone("mom_nightVisit")>>
		<div>
			<<link "Ask what happens at six">>
				<<replace "#mom-calendar-choice">>
					<<silently>>
					<<set _msgs to [
						{ who: $player, text: "And what happens at six?" },
						{ who: $mom, text: "You come home. You eat something with a vegetable in it. And then you..." },
						{ text: "She looks at the red block. I watch her hear the sentence before she's said the rest of it." },
						{ who: $mom, text: "...and then you relax. That's all I meant. You relax, honey. Like a normal person." },
						{ who: $player, text: "Sure." },
						{ who: $mom, text: "Don't 'sure' me." },
					]>>
					<</silently>>
					<<Chat _msgs>>
					<p>She takes the tablet and walks back to her desk a little faster than she came. She doesn't delete anything. At five to six, a reminder pops up on my screen that she must have added afterwards. It only says: <i>don't be late.</i></p>
					<<UpdateStat "+" "MomRelation" 1>>
					<<UpdateStat "+" "MomLust" 2>>
				<</replace>>
			<</link>>
		</div>
	<</if>>
</div>
